# Copy to .env.local for local development. Never commit .env.local.
#
# Municipality identity (name, coordinates, domain, branding) does NOT belong
# here — it lives in config/lgu.config.json, read through src/lib/lgu-config.ts.
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* values reach the browser. Never put a secret behind
# that prefix.

# Base URL used by Playwright when running E2E against a deployed target.
# PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# The visitor counter's key-value store (TAGO-116). BOTH ARE SECRET — never
# prefix either with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Absent here as values on purpose: this file
# is the committed template and carries names only.
#
# With neither set, the counter renders nothing and the portal is otherwise
# completely normal — that is the designed state for a developer machine and
# for any preview build, not a misconfiguration.
#
# No IP address, user agent or identifier of any kind is stored by the counter.
# If that ever changes it is a governance decision with a privacy policy
# attached, not an edit to this file.
# VISITOR_STORE_URL=
# VISITOR_STORE_TOKEN=

# ⚠️ PREVIEW ONLY — a STAND-IN visitor count, so the footer can be looked at
# before a store exists. It publishes a number that is not true, which is the
# one thing this portal is built never to do.
#
# A real store ALWAYS wins: with VISITOR_STORE_URL and VISITOR_STORE_TOKEN set,
# this is never read and cannot override a live count. Delete it from any
# environment the day a store is provisioned.
# VISITOR_COUNT_PREVIEW=12480
